}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "categoryId": 4,
    "name": "Beach Towel",
    "code": "beach-towel",
    "price": 24.95,
    "stock": 40,
    "img": [
      "https://picsum.photos/seed/lpa-beach-towel/640/640"
    ],
    "description": "Quick-dry towel for Gold Coast beaches."
  }
}

docs {
  # Create a product

  The store catalogue. Every product belongs to a category, returned inline as `category: { id, name, code }`.

  The server fills `created` with an audit stamp (`client`, `server`, `serverDate`, `serverTime` in APP_TIMEZONE, `unixTime`, `user`, `role` from the token). `status`, `statusName`, `created`, `updated`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` and any other undeclared key are ignored if sent. An optional top-level `time` (ISO string) is recorded as `created.client`.

  ## Auth

  Bearer token of a user whose role is `ADMIN` (send **auth/Log in** first; it stores `{{token}}`).

  ## Body (JSON)

  | Field | Type | Required | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `categoryId` | integer | yes on create | Id of an existing category. |
  | `name` | string | yes on create | 1–150 characters; unique. |
  | `code` | string | yes on create | Lowercase letters, digits and hyphens; unique; max 60. |
  | `price` | number | yes on create | Price in AUD; ≥ 0. |
  | `stock` | integer | no | Units in stock; ≥ 0; defaults to 0 on create, unchanged on update when omitted. |
  | `img` | string[] (URLs) | no | Up to 10 image URLs; defaults to [] on create, unchanged on update when omitted. |
  | `description` | string \| null | no | Max 5000 characters. |

  ## Responses

  ### 201 Created

    {
      "message": "Product created",
      "data": {
        "id": 1,
        "categoryId": 4,
        "name": "Beach Towel",
        "code": "beach-towel",
        "price": 24.95,
        "stock": 40,
        "img": [
          "https://picsum.photos/seed/lpa-beach-towel/640/640"
        ],
        "description": "Quick-dry towel for Gold Coast beaches.",
        "category": {
          "id": 4,
          "name": "Sports",
          "code": "sports"
        },
        "created": {
          "client": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "server": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "serverDate": "2026-09-27",
          "serverTime": "12:30:14",
          "unixTime": 1790476214,
          "user": 1,
          "role": "ADMIN"
        },
        "updated": null,
        "statusName": "ACTIVE",
        "status": 1,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z"
      },
      "pagination": null
    }

  ### 400 Bad Request — validation failed

  A body field is missing or invalid; one `errors` entry per field. Also returned when a referenced id does not exist (`categoryId`).

    {
      "message": "Some fields need attention.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": [
        {
          "field": "categoryId",
          "message": "Invalid input"
        }
      ]
    }

  ### 401 Unauthorized — missing, invalid or expired token

    {
      "message": "Sign in to continue.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  ### 403 Forbidden — the token's role is not ADMIN

    {
      "message": "You do not have permission to do this.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  ### 409 Conflict — a unique field is already in use

  Unique fields: `name`, `code`. Soft-deleted records still hold their values.

    {
      "message": "A record with this name already exists.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": [
        {
          "field": "name",
          "message": "name is already in use."
        }
      ]
    }

  Outside production, error bodies also carry `stack`.
}
